IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc11-definitions`

-- ccc11-offences.l4 -- Part VIII.1 (Offences Relating to Conveyances), sections 320.13 to 320.18 (the offences) of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46.
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively, from the text alone. Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation
-- (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- Each function answers a MAYBE BOOLEAN: JUST TRUE (the case is within the section on the text's words); JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words); NOTHING (not covered).
-- A term of section 2 or of section 320.11 is taken as an INPUT named for its section ("..., by s 2 motor vehicle"), typed as the answering section answers (MAYBE BOOLEAN),
-- so a NOTHING among the inputs is carried through and never turned into FALSE. The "who" of "Everyone commits an offence who ..." is read as the section's own definition
-- of the offence: an element that is missing is the section's no (marginal reading (a) in NOTES.md, which also states the other reading).
-- The punishment of each offence is in ccc11-punishment.l4 (sections 320.19 to 320.21); the exceptions of 320.14(5) to (7) and 320.18(2) are encoded here, beside the offences they qualify.

-- Line 6207: the division heading "Offences and Punishment": inert (reason 1, a heading).
-- src:6207 | Offences and Punishment
§ `Part VIII.1 -- section 320.13: dangerous operation`

-- src:6208 | Dangerous operation
-- src:6209 | 320.13 (1) Everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance in a manner that, having regard to all of the circumstances, is dangerous to the public.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.13(1) (src:6208-6209)
GIVEN `the person operated a conveyance, by s 320.11 the person operates the conveyance` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the manner of operation was, having regard to all of the circumstances, dangerous to the public` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.13(1) everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance in a manner that is dangerous to the public` MEANS
    IF NOT `the manner of operation was, having regard to all of the circumstances, dangerous to the public`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance in a manner that, having regard to all of the circumstances, is dangerous to the public"
    ELSE `the person operated a conveyance, by s 320.11 the person operates the conveyance`   -- JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE for "operates a conveyance" unmet (s 320.11 "operate means"); NOTHING when that is not covered

-- src:6210 | Operation causing bodily harm
-- src:6211 | (2) Everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance in a manner that, having regard to all of the circumstances, is dangerous to the public and, as a result, causes bodily harm to another person.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.13(2) (src:6210-6211)
GIVEN `the person operated a conveyance, by s 320.11 the person operates the conveyance` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the manner of operation was, having regard to all of the circumstances, dangerous to the public` IS A BOOLEAN
      `as a result, the person caused harm to another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the harm was bodily harm, by s 2 bodily harm` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.13(2) everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance dangerously and, as a result, causes bodily harm to another person` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the manner of operation was, having regard to all of the circumstances, dangerous to the public`) OR (NOT `as a result, the person caused harm to another person`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance in a manner that, having regard to all of the circumstances, is dangerous to the public and, as a result, causes bodily harm to another person"
    ELSE `s 320.11 helper: both hold` `the person operated a conveyance, by s 320.11 the person operates the conveyance` `the harm was bodily harm, by s 2 bodily harm`
    -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): an input that the answering section leaves not covered gives NOTHING (carried through the Kleene helper)

-- src:6212 | Operation causing death
-- src:6213 | (3) Everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance in a manner that, having regard to all of the circumstances, is dangerous to the public and, as a result, causes the death of another person.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.13(3) (src:6212-6213)
GIVEN `the person operated a conveyance, by s 320.11 the person operates the conveyance` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the manner of operation was, having regard to all of the circumstances, dangerous to the public` IS A BOOLEAN
      `as a result, the person caused the death of another person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.13(3) everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance dangerously and, as a result, causes the death of another person` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the manner of operation was, having regard to all of the circumstances, dangerous to the public`) OR (NOT `as a result, the person caused the death of another person`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance in a manner that, having regard to all of the circumstances, is dangerous to the public and, as a result, causes the death of another person"
    ELSE `the person operated a conveyance, by s 320.11 the person operates the conveyance`

§ `Part VIII.1 -- section 320.14: operation while impaired`

-- 320.14(1) is the composition of its four paragraphs: a person commits the offence if any of (a) to (d) holds. The four answers are inputs, taken from the four functions below.
-- src:6214 | Operation while impaired
-- src:6215 | 320.14 (1) Everyone commits an offence who
-- src:6216 | (a) operates a conveyance while the person’s ability to operate it is impaired to any degree by alcohol or a drug or by a combination of alcohol and a drug;
-- src:6217 | (b) subject to subsection (5), has, within two hours after ceasing to operate a conveyance, a blood alcohol concentration that is equal to or exceeds 80 mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood;
-- src:6218 | (c) subject to subsection (6), has, within two hours after ceasing to operate a conveyance, a blood drug concentration that is equal to or exceeds the blood drug concentration for the drug that is prescribed by regulation; or
-- src:6219 | (d) subject to subsection (7), has, within two hours after ceasing to operate a conveyance, a blood alcohol concentration and a blood drug concentration that is equal to or exceeds the blood alcohol concentration and the blood drug concentration for the drug that are prescribed by regulation for instances where alcohol and that drug are combined.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.14(1) (src:6214-6219)
GIVEN `paragraph (a): impaired operation, by s 320.14(1)(a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (b): blood alcohol concentration, by s 320.14(1)(b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (c): blood drug concentration, by s 320.14(1)(c)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (d): alcohol and drug combined, by s 320.14(1)(d)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.14(1) everyone commits an offence under subsection 320.14(1)` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Everyone commits an offence who (a) operates a conveyance while the person’s ability to operate it is impaired to any degree by alcohol or a drug or by a combination of alcohol and a drug; (b) ... (c) ... or (d) ..."
    `s 320.11 helper: either holds`
        (`s 320.11 helper: either holds` `paragraph (a): impaired operation, by s 320.14(1)(a)` `paragraph (b): blood alcohol concentration, by s 320.14(1)(b)`)
        (`s 320.11 helper: either holds` `paragraph (c): blood drug concentration, by s 320.14(1)(c)` `paragraph (d): alcohol and drug combined, by s 320.14(1)(d)`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): an input that the answering section leaves not covered gives NOTHING (carried through the Kleene helper)

@ref Criminal Code s 320.14(1)(a) (src:6216)
GIVEN `the person operated a conveyance, by s 320.11 the person operates the conveyance` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person’s ability to operate the conveyance was impaired to any degree by alcohol or a drug or by a combination of alcohol and a drug` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.14(1)(a) everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance while their ability to operate it is impaired to any degree by alcohol or a drug` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person’s ability to operate the conveyance was impaired to any degree by alcohol or a drug or by a combination of alcohol and a drug`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "operates a conveyance while the person’s ability to operate it is impaired to any degree by alcohol or a drug or by a combination of alcohol and a drug"
    ELSE `the person operated a conveyance, by s 320.11 the person operates the conveyance`

-- (b): "subject to subsection (5)". The concentration is the one the person HAS, at some moment within two hours after ceasing to operate; where the sample was taken later,
-- section 320.31(4) is what fixes it (ccc11-evidence.l4), and its answer is what is passed here. The exception is the answer of s 320.14(5).
@ref Criminal Code s 320.14(1)(b) (src:6217)
GIVEN `the person operated a conveyance, by s 320.11 the person operates the conveyance` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person’s blood alcohol concentration at some time within two hours after ceasing to operate the conveyance, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` IS A NUMBER
      `the exception in subsection 320.14(5) applies, by s 320.14(5)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.14(1)(b) everyone commits an offence who has, within two hours after ceasing to operate a conveyance, a blood alcohol concentration of 80 mg or more` MEANS
    IF `the person’s blood alcohol concentration at some time within two hours after ceasing to operate the conveyance, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` LESS THAN 80
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "has, within two hours after ceasing to operate a conveyance, a blood alcohol concentration that is equal to or exceeds 80 mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood"
    ELSE `s 320.11 helper: both hold`
             `the person operated a conveyance, by s 320.11 the person operates the conveyance`
             (`s 320.11 helper: the opposite of` `the exception in subsection 320.14(5) applies, by s 320.14(5)`)
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person commits an offence under paragraph (1)(b) if" (the exception applies)
    -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): an input that the answering section leaves not covered gives NOTHING (carried through the Kleene helper)

-- (c): "subject to subsection (6)". The prescribed concentration is set by regulation (paragraph 320.38(b)), which is not among the sources: an input.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.14(1)(c) (src:6218)
GIVEN `the person operated a conveyance, by s 320.11 the person operates the conveyance` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person’s blood drug concentration for the drug at some time within two hours after ceasing to operate the conveyance` IS A NUMBER
      `the blood drug concentration for the drug that is prescribed by regulation for the purposes of paragraph 320.14(1)(c), in the same units` IS A NUMBER
      `the exception in subsection 320.14(6) applies, by s 320.14(6)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.14(1)(c) everyone commits an offence who has, within two hours after ceasing to operate a conveyance, a blood drug concentration at or above the prescribed concentration` MEANS
    IF `the person’s blood drug concentration for the drug at some time within two hours after ceasing to operate the conveyance` LESS THAN `the blood drug concentration for the drug that is prescribed by regulation for the purposes of paragraph 320.14(1)(c), in the same units`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a blood drug concentration that is equal to or exceeds the blood drug concentration for the drug that is prescribed by regulation"
    ELSE `s 320.11 helper: both hold`
             `the person operated a conveyance, by s 320.11 the person operates the conveyance`
             (`s 320.11 helper: the opposite of` `the exception in subsection 320.14(6) applies, by s 320.14(6)`)
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person commits an offence under paragraph (1)(c) or subsection (4) if" (the exception applies)
    -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): an input that the answering section leaves not covered gives NOTHING (carried through the Kleene helper)

-- (d): "subject to subsection (7)". Both prescribed concentrations are set by regulation (paragraph 320.38(c)): inputs.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.14(1)(d) (src:6219)
GIVEN `the person operated a conveyance, by s 320.11 the person operates the conveyance` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person’s blood alcohol concentration at some time within two hours after ceasing to operate the conveyance, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` IS A NUMBER
      `the person’s blood drug concentration for the drug at the same time` IS A NUMBER
      `the blood alcohol concentration prescribed by regulation for instances where alcohol and that drug are combined (paragraph 320.38(c))` IS A NUMBER
      `the blood drug concentration prescribed by regulation for instances where alcohol and that drug are combined (paragraph 320.38(c))` IS A NUMBER
      `the exception in subsection 320.14(7) applies, by s 320.14(7)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.14(1)(d) everyone commits an offence who has, within two hours after ceasing to operate a conveyance, alcohol and drug concentrations at or above those prescribed for the combination` MEANS
    IF `the person’s blood alcohol concentration at some time within two hours after ceasing to operate the conveyance, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` LESS THAN `the blood alcohol concentration prescribed by regulation for instances where alcohol and that drug are combined (paragraph 320.38(c))`
       OR `the person’s blood drug concentration for the drug at the same time` LESS THAN `the blood drug concentration prescribed by regulation for instances where alcohol and that drug are combined (paragraph 320.38(c))`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a blood alcohol concentration and a blood drug concentration that is equal to or exceeds the blood alcohol concentration and the blood drug concentration for the drug that are prescribed by regulation for instances where alcohol and that drug are combined"
    ELSE `s 320.11 helper: both hold`
             `the person operated a conveyance, by s 320.11 the person operates the conveyance`
             (`s 320.11 helper: the opposite of` `the exception in subsection 320.14(7) applies, by s 320.14(7)`)
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person commits an offence under paragraph (1)(d) if" (the exception applies)
    -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): an input that the answering section leaves not covered gives NOTHING (carried through the Kleene helper)

-- (2): "commits an offence under subsection (1) and who, while operating the conveyance, causes bodily harm to another person".
-- src:6220 | Operation causing bodily harm
-- src:6221 | (2) Everyone commits an offence who commits an offence under subsection (1) and who, while operating the conveyance, causes bodily harm to another person.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.14(2) (src:6220-6221)
GIVEN `the person commits an offence under subsection 320.14(1), by s 320.14(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `while operating the conveyance, the person caused harm to another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the harm was bodily harm, by s 2 bodily harm` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.14(2) everyone commits an offence who commits an offence under subsection 320.14(1) and, while operating the conveyance, causes bodily harm to another person` MEANS
    IF NOT `while operating the conveyance, the person caused harm to another person`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Everyone commits an offence who commits an offence under subsection (1) and who, while operating the conveyance, causes bodily harm to another person"
    ELSE `s 320.11 helper: both hold` `the person commits an offence under subsection 320.14(1), by s 320.14(1)` `the harm was bodily harm, by s 2 bodily harm`
    -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): an input that the answering section leaves not covered gives NOTHING (carried through the Kleene helper)

-- src:6222 | Operation causing death
-- src:6223 | (3) Everyone commits an offence who commits an offence under subsection (1) and who, while operating the conveyance, causes the death of another person.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.14(3) (src:6222-6223)
GIVEN `the person commits an offence under subsection 320.14(1), by s 320.14(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `while operating the conveyance, the person caused the death of another person` IS A BOOLEAN
