-- (4): "Subject to subsection (6)". Two prescribed concentrations (paragraphs 320.38(d) and 320.38(b)), both set by regulation: inputs. The person's concentration must be at or above
-- the first and below the second.
-- src:6224 | Operation — low blood drug concentration
-- src:6225 | (4) Subject to subsection (6), everyone commits an offence who has, within two hours after ceasing to operate a conveyance, a blood drug concentration that is equal to or exceeds the blood drug concentration for the drug that is prescribed by regulation and that is less than the concentration prescribed for the purposes of paragraph (1)(c).
@ref Criminal Code s 320.14(4) (src:6224-6225)
GIVEN `the person operated a conveyance, by s 320.11 the person operates the conveyance` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person’s blood drug concentration for the drug at some time within two hours after ceasing to operate the conveyance` IS A NUMBER
      `the blood drug concentration for the drug that is prescribed by regulation for the purposes of subsection 320.14(4) (paragraph 320.38(d)), in the same units` IS A NUMBER
      `the concentration prescribed for the purposes of paragraph 320.14(1)(c) (paragraph 320.38(b)), in the same units` IS A NUMBER
      `the exception in subsection 320.14(6) applies, by s 320.14(6)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.14(4) everyone commits an offence who has, within two hours after ceasing to operate a conveyance, a low blood drug concentration` MEANS
    IF `the person’s blood drug concentration for the drug at some time within two hours after ceasing to operate the conveyance` LESS THAN `the blood drug concentration for the drug that is prescribed by regulation for the purposes of subsection 320.14(4) (paragraph 320.38(d)), in the same units`
       OR `the person’s blood drug concentration for the drug at some time within two hours after ceasing to operate the conveyance` AT LEAST `the concentration prescribed for the purposes of paragraph 320.14(1)(c) (paragraph 320.38(b)), in the same units`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a blood drug concentration that is equal to or exceeds the blood drug concentration for the drug that is prescribed by regulation and that is less than the concentration prescribed for the purposes of paragraph (1)(c)"
    ELSE `s 320.11 helper: both hold`
             `the person operated a conveyance, by s 320.11 the person operates the conveyance`
             (`s 320.11 helper: the opposite of` `the exception in subsection 320.14(6) applies, by s 320.14(6)`)
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person commits an offence under paragraph (1)(c) or subsection (4) if" (the exception applies)
    -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): an input that the answering section leaves not covered gives NOTHING (carried through the Kleene helper)

-- (5): the exception answers "does this subsection give an exception on these facts": JUST TRUE when (a), (b) and (c) all hold; JUST FALSE when one of them fails, because the text
-- introduces the exception with "if" (marginal reading (a)); the answer is NEVER "the person commits the offence". Paragraph (c) has two limbs ("consistent with ... and with ...").
-- src:6226 | Exception — alcohol
-- src:6227 | (5) No person commits an offence under paragraph (1)(b) if
-- src:6228 | (a) they consumed alcohol after ceasing to operate the conveyance;
-- src:6229 | (b) after ceasing to operate the conveyance, they had no reasonable expectation that they would be required to provide a sample of breath or blood; and
-- src:6230 | (c) their alcohol consumption is consistent with their blood alcohol concentration as determined in accordance with subsection 320.31(1) or (2) and with their having had, at the time when they were operating the conveyance, a blood alcohol concentration that was less than 80 mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.14(5) (src:6226-6230)
GIVEN `the person consumed alcohol after ceasing to operate the conveyance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `after ceasing to operate the conveyance, the person had no reasonable expectation that they would be required to provide a sample of breath or blood` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person’s alcohol consumption is consistent with their blood alcohol concentration as determined in accordance with subsection 320.31(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person’s alcohol consumption is consistent with their having had, at the time when they were operating the conveyance, a blood alcohol concentration that was less than 80 mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.14(5) the exception applies: no person commits an offence under paragraph 320.14(1)(b)` MEANS
    IF `the person consumed alcohol after ceasing to operate the conveyance`
       AND `after ceasing to operate the conveyance, the person had no reasonable expectation that they would be required to provide a sample of breath or blood`
       AND `the person’s alcohol consumption is consistent with their blood alcohol concentration as determined in accordance with subsection 320.31(1) or (2)`
       AND `the person’s alcohol consumption is consistent with their having had, at the time when they were operating the conveyance, a blood alcohol concentration that was less than 80 mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person commits an offence under paragraph (1)(b) if" (an "if" condition unmet: this subsection gives no exception on these facts)

