§ `Part VIII.1 -- section 320.15: failure or refusal to comply with a demand`

-- (1): the demand must be "a demand made under section 320.27 or 320.28": whether it was is the answer of those sections (ccc11-investigation.l4), taken as an input; NOTHING stays NOTHING.
-- src:6240 | Failure or refusal to comply with demand
-- src:6241 | 320.15 (1) Everyone commits an offence who, knowing that a demand has been made, fails or refuses to comply, without reasonable excuse, with a demand made under section 320.27 or 320.28.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.15(1) (src:6240-6241)
GIVEN `the person knew that a demand had been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person failed or refused to comply with the demand` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the demand was made under section 320.27 or 320.28, by s 320.27 and s 320.28` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.15(1) everyone commits an offence who, knowing that a demand has been made, fails or refuses to comply with it without reasonable excuse` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the person knew that a demand had been made`) OR (NOT `the person failed or refused to comply with the demand`) OR `the person had a reasonable excuse`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Everyone commits an offence who, knowing that a demand has been made, fails or refuses to comply, without reasonable excuse, with a demand made under section 320.27 or 320.28"
    ELSE `the demand was made under section 320.27 or 320.28, by s 320.27 and s 320.28`

-- (2) and (3): the knowledge or recklessness is one phrase of the text and is asked as the text words it; no separate "the accident in fact resulted in" element is added (fork F6 in NOTES.md).
-- src:6242 | Accident resulting in bodily harm
-- src:6243 | (2) Everyone commits an offence who commits an offence under subsection (1) and who, at the time of the failure or refusal, knows that, or is reckless as to whether, they were involved in an accident that resulted in bodily harm to another person.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.15(2) (src:6242-6243)
GIVEN `the person commits an offence under subsection 320.15(1), by s 320.15(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `at the time of the failure or refusal, the person knew that, or was reckless as to whether, they were involved in an accident that resulted in bodily harm to another person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.15(2) everyone commits an offence who commits an offence under subsection 320.15(1) and knows that, or is reckless as to whether, they were involved in an accident that resulted in bodily harm` MEANS
    IF NOT `at the time of the failure or refusal, the person knew that, or was reckless as to whether, they were involved in an accident that resulted in bodily harm to another person`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Everyone commits an offence who commits an offence under subsection (1) and who, at the time of the failure or refusal, knows that, or is reckless as to whether, they were involved in an accident that resulted in bodily harm to another person"
    ELSE `the person commits an offence under subsection 320.15(1), by s 320.15(1)`

-- src:6244 | Accident resulting in death
-- src:6245 | (3) Everyone commits an offence who commits an offence under subsection (1) and who, at the time of the failure or refusal, knows that, or is reckless as to whether, they were involved in an accident that resulted in the death of another person or in bodily harm to another person whose death ensues.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.15(3) (src:6244-6245)
GIVEN `the person commits an offence under subsection 320.15(1), by s 320.15(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `at the time of the failure or refusal, the person knew that, or was reckless as to whether, they were involved in an accident that resulted in the death of another person or in bodily harm to another person whose death ensues` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.15(3) everyone commits an offence who commits an offence under subsection 320.15(1) and knows that, or is reckless as to whether, they were involved in an accident that resulted in death` MEANS
    IF NOT `at the time of the failure or refusal, the person knew that, or was reckless as to whether, they were involved in an accident that resulted in the death of another person or in bodily harm to another person whose death ensues`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Everyone commits an offence who commits an offence under subsection (1) and who, at the time of the failure or refusal, knows that, or is reckless as to whether, they were involved in an accident that resulted in the death of another person or in bodily harm to another person whose death ensues"
    ELSE `the person commits an offence under subsection 320.15(1), by s 320.15(1)`

-- (4): a bar. JUST TRUE = the person is barred from a second conviction under section 320.15 for the same transaction; JUST FALSE when the conditions of the bar are not met
-- ("is convicted of an offence under this section"; "another offence under this section"; "the same transaction"): the bar is the provision's own question (marginal reading (a)).
-- src:6246 | Only one conviction
-- src:6247 | (4) A person who is convicted of an offence under this section is not to be convicted of another offence under this section with respect to the same transaction.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.15(4) (src:6246-6247)
GIVEN `the person is convicted of an offence under section 320.15` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other offence is an offence under section 320.15` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other offence is with respect to the same transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.15(4) the person is barred from being convicted of another offence under section 320.15 with respect to the same transaction` MEANS
    IF `the person is convicted of an offence under section 320.15` AND `the other offence is an offence under section 320.15` AND `the other offence is with respect to the same transaction`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person who is convicted of an offence under this section is not to be convicted of another offence under this section with respect to the same transaction" (the bar's conditions unmet)

§ `Part VIII.1 -- section 320.16: failure to stop after an accident`

-- (1): "fails, without reasonable excuse, to stop the conveyance, give their name and address and, if any person has been injured or appears to require assistance, offer assistance".
-- Reading taken (fork F7): the person fails if they fail to do ANY ONE of the things listed (stop; give name and address; offer assistance where a person is injured or appears to need it).
-- src:6248 | Failure to stop after accident
-- src:6249 | 320.16 (1) Everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance and who at the time of operating the conveyance knows that, or is reckless as to whether, the conveyance has been involved in an accident with a person or another conveyance and who fails, without reasonable excuse, to stop the conveyance, give their name and address and, if any person has been injured or appears to require assistance, offer assistance.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.16(1) (src:6248-6249)
GIVEN `the person operated a conveyance, by s 320.11 the person operates the conveyance` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `at the time of operating the conveyance the person knew that, or was reckless as to whether, the conveyance had been involved in an accident with a person or another conveyance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person failed to stop the conveyance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person failed to give their name and address` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a person was injured or appeared to require assistance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person failed to offer assistance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.16(1) everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance, knows that or is reckless as to whether it has been involved in an accident, and fails without reasonable excuse to stop, give their name and address and offer assistance` MEANS
    IF (NOT `at the time of operating the conveyance the person knew that, or was reckless as to whether, the conveyance had been involved in an accident with a person or another conveyance`)
       OR `the person had a reasonable excuse`
       OR (NOT (`the person failed to stop the conveyance` OR `the person failed to give their name and address` OR (`a person was injured or appeared to require assistance` AND `the person failed to offer assistance`)))
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance and who at the time of operating the conveyance knows that, or is reckless as to whether, the conveyance has been involved in an accident with a person or another conveyance and who fails, without reasonable excuse, to stop the conveyance, give their name and address and, if any person has been injured or appears to require assistance, offer assistance"
    ELSE `the person operated a conveyance, by s 320.11 the person operates the conveyance`

-- src:6250 | Accident resulting in bodily harm
-- src:6251 | (2) Everyone commits an offence who commits an offence under subsection (1) and who at the time of committing the offence knows that, or is reckless as to whether, the accident resulted in bodily harm to another person.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.16(2) (src:6250-6251)
