      `at the time of committing the offence the person knew that, or was reckless as to whether, the accident resulted in bodily harm to another person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.16(2) everyone commits an offence who commits an offence under subsection 320.16(1) and knows that, or is reckless as to whether, the accident resulted in bodily harm` MEANS
    IF NOT `at the time of committing the offence the person knew that, or was reckless as to whether, the accident resulted in bodily harm to another person`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Everyone commits an offence who commits an offence under subsection (1) and who at the time of committing the offence knows that, or is reckless as to whether, the accident resulted in bodily harm to another person"
    ELSE `the person commits an offence under subsection 320.16(1), by s 320.16(1)`

-- src:6252 | Accident resulting in death
