    ELSE `the person commits an offence under subsection 320.16(1), by s 320.16(1)`

§ `Part VIII.1 -- section 320.17: flight from a peace officer`

-- src:6254 | Flight from peace officer
-- src:6255 | 320.17 Everyone commits an offence who operates a motor vehicle or vessel while being pursued by a peace officer and who fails, without reasonable excuse, to stop the motor vehicle or vessel as soon as is reasonable in the circumstances.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.17 (src:6254-6255)
GIVEN `the person operated a conveyance, by s 320.11 the person operates the conveyance` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the conveyance was a motor vehicle, by s 2 motor vehicle` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the conveyance was a vessel, by s 320.11 the thing is a vessel` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person was being pursued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the pursuer was a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person failed to stop as soon as is reasonable in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.17 everyone commits an offence who operates a motor vehicle or vessel while being pursued by a peace officer and fails without reasonable excuse to stop` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the person was being pursued`) OR (NOT `the person failed to stop as soon as is reasonable in the circumstances`) OR `the person had a reasonable excuse`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Everyone commits an offence who operates a motor vehicle or vessel while being pursued by a peace officer and who fails, without reasonable excuse, to stop the motor vehicle or vessel as soon as is reasonable in the circumstances"
    ELSE `s 320.11 helper: both hold`
             `the person operated a conveyance, by s 320.11 the person operates the conveyance`
             (`s 320.11 helper: both hold`
                 (`s 320.11 helper: either holds` `the conveyance was a motor vehicle, by s 2 motor vehicle` `the conveyance was a vessel, by s 320.11 the thing is a vessel`)
                 `the pursuer was a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): an input that the answering section leaves not covered gives NOTHING (carried through the Kleene helper)

§ `Part VIII.1 -- section 320.18: operation while prohibited`

-- (1): paragraphs (a) and (b) are two ways of being "prohibited from doing so": an order made under the Criminal Code, or another legal restriction imposed in respect of a conviction under
-- the Code or a discharge under section 730. "Subsection (2)" is an exception: its answer is an input.
-- src:6256 | Operation while prohibited
-- src:6257 | 320.18 (1) Everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance while prohibited from doing so
-- src:6258 | (a) by an order made under this Act; or
-- src:6259 | (b) by any other form of legal restriction imposed under any other Act of Parliament or under provincial law in respect of a conviction under this Act or a discharge under section 730.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.18(1) (src:6256-6259)
GIVEN `the person operated a conveyance, by s 320.11 the person operates the conveyance` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person was prohibited from operating a conveyance by an order made under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was prohibited by any other form of legal restriction imposed under any other Act of Parliament or under provincial law in respect of a conviction under this Act or a discharge under section 730` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exception in subsection 320.18(2) applies, by s 320.18(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.18(1) everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance while prohibited from doing so` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the person was prohibited from operating a conveyance by an order made under this Act` OR `the person was prohibited by any other form of legal restriction imposed under any other Act of Parliament or under provincial law in respect of a conviction under this Act or a discharge under section 730`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance while prohibited from doing so (a) by an order made under this Act; or (b) by any other form of legal restriction"
    ELSE `s 320.11 helper: both hold`
             `the person operated a conveyance, by s 320.11 the person operates the conveyance`
             (`s 320.11 helper: the opposite of` `the exception in subsection 320.18(2) applies, by s 320.18(2)`)
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person commits an offence under subsection (1) arising out of the operation of a motor vehicle if" (the exception applies)
    -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): an input that the answering section leaves not covered gives NOTHING (carried through the Kleene helper)

-- src:6260 | Exception
-- src:6261 | (2) No person commits an offence under subsection (1) arising out of the operation of a motor vehicle if they are registered in an alcohol ignition interlock device program established under the law of the province in which they reside and they comply with the conditions of the program.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.18(2) (src:6260-6261)
GIVEN `the operation was of a motor vehicle, by s 2 motor vehicle` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is registered in an alcohol ignition interlock device program established under the law of the province in which they reside` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person complies with the conditions of the program` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.18(2) the exception applies: no person commits an offence under subsection 320.18(1) arising out of the operation of a motor vehicle` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the person is registered in an alcohol ignition interlock device program established under the law of the province in which they reside` AND `the person complies with the conditions of the program`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person commits an offence under subsection (1) arising out of the operation of a motor vehicle if they are registered in an alcohol ignition interlock device program established under the law of the province in which they reside and they comply with the conditions of the program" (an "if" condition unmet: this subsection gives no exception on these facts)
    ELSE `the operation was of a motor vehicle, by s 2 motor vehicle`   -- JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE or NOTHING as s 2 "motor vehicle" answers
